      "math_academy_id": "q-19194",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Let $a=⟨-2,-1,-4⟩$ and $b=⟨6,-5,3⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 6+(-1)\\cdot (-5)+(-4)\\cdot 3}{{6}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{3}^{2}}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{19}{70}⟨6,-5,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{57}{35},\\frac{19}{14},-\\frac{57}{70}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
